From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:28:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] webkit: check provider availability as the system

SystemImpl.getWebViewPackages() drops the configured providers that are not
installed. It asks the package manager with MATCH_ANY_USER, and the binder
methods getAllWebViewPackages() and getValidWebViewPackages() run that check
under the identity of the calling application, which the package manager
rejects without INTERACT_ACROSS_USERS ("MATCH_ANY_USER flag requires
INTERACT_ACROSS_USERS permission"). The configured list is public and AOSP
returns it to any caller of getAllWebViewPackages().

Whether a provider is installed does not depend on who asks, so run the
availability check as the system. getValidWebViewPackages() still reads each
provider's package info as the caller, and so still needs the permission, as
on AOSP.
---
 .../core/java/com/android/server/webkit/SystemImpl.java    | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/webkit/SystemImpl.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/webkit/SystemImpl.java
index c7f8185549f74347c3702fe5265cd6370c121f49..a8397a23405d12afccd2e6ebebf3541bb602551a 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/webkit/SystemImpl.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/webkit/SystemImpl.java
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ import android.content.pm.PackageInstaller;
 import android.content.pm.PackageManager;
 import android.content.pm.PackageManager.NameNotFoundException;
 import android.content.res.XmlResourceParser;
+import android.os.Binder;
 import android.os.Build;
 import android.os.RemoteException;
 import android.os.UserHandle;
@@ -154,11 +155,17 @@ public class SystemImpl implements SystemInterface {
     }
 
     private boolean isProviderAvailable(WebViewProviderInfo configInfo) {
+        // getWebViewPackages() serves binder callers that are ordinary applications. They may not
+        // query packages across users, which PACKAGE_FLAGS asks for (MATCH_ANY_USER), and whether
+        // a provider is installed does not depend on who asks.
+        final long token = Binder.clearCallingIdentity();
         try {
             getPackageInfoForProvider(configInfo);
             return true;
         } catch (NameNotFoundException e) {
             return false;
+        } finally {
+            Binder.restoreCallingIdentity(token);
         }
     }
 
